/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  bubble01_reaction_mass_boiling_point -- the BOILING POINT OF A REACTION
  MASS, which is what the thermal-safety methodology takes as the technical
  limit MTT of an open vessel at atmospheric pressure.

  The mass is the one in tutorials/batch/reactor/batch26_cooling_failure
  (and batch27, the same reaction dosed): acetic acid, ethanol, ethyl
  acetate and water.  constant/ is a COPY of batch26's sealed constant/
  (the same records under the same manifest, the same thermoPhysPropDict;
  only the reactor's own constant/reactions is left out, because no
  property operation reads it), so the boiling point below is computed on
  exactly the thermodynamics the reactor case declares: an IDEAL liquid
  (Raoult, gamma = 1) over an ideal gas.

  The composition is the reactor's at batch26's shipped cooling failure
  (t_f = 600 s; mole fractions of the trajectory row at 600 s, 39.3 % of
  the ethanol converted).  The process-safety EduTool rewrites the four
  lines with the reactor contents at the failure instant the reader
  chooses, read from the engine's own trajectory, and reads T_bubble back.
  ONE KEY PER LINE: the GUI's override anchors on a key at the start of a
  line, so a composition written on one line is a knob that silently
  misses.

  WHAT THIS IS NOT.  The real quaternary is far from ideal -- ethyl
  acetate, ethanol and water form azeotropes that boil below every pure
  component -- so the ideal bubble point is the reactor case's own model
  answer, not a measured boiling point.  And it is a bubble point at the
  failure instant: as a runaway converts the mass, its composition, and so
  its boiling point, moves.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name        reactionMassBubblePoint;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state
        {
            T       330 K;          // T_p; the bubble point does not depend on it
            P       1.013 bar;      // the reactor's pressure (batch26 0/internalStates/reactor)
            composition
            {
                aceticAcid      0.303502;
                ethanol         0.303502;
                ethylAcetate    0.196498;
                water           0.196498;
            }
        }
        properties  ( T_bubble );
    }
);
